* Merkle Patricia\nForestry (Cardano)
** Structure
*** Radix-16 Patricia trie
*** Path = blake2b-256(key)\n64 nibbles, uniform
*** Two node kinds only:\nBranch and Leaf
*** Branch = h(nibbles(prefix) || M)
*** Leaf = h(head || tail || h(value))
*** Empty trie = 32 zero bytes
** The forestry idea
*** 16 children merkleised\ninto a depth-4 binary tree
*** 4 sibling hashes per level\ninstead of 15
*** 128 bytes per branch step
*** Cached null_hash_2 / _4 / _8
*** Costs CPU and memory,\nbuys proof bytes
left side
** Proof format
*** Branch { skip, neighbors }
*** Fork { skip, neighbor }
*** Leaf { skip, key, value }
*** skip = shared prefix length
*** Processed left to right
** Two roots, one proof
*** including() -> with the item
*** excluding() -> without it
*** insert, delete, update, has, miss
*** Proof binds to one exact root
** Versus other trees
*** Binary Merkle: index, no exclusion
*** Sparse Merkle: 256 deep, binary
*** Ethereum MPT: ~15 hashes/level
*** MPF at 10^6 items: ~760 bytes
@endmindmap
